<title>SINGAPORE: India issues second Jan diesel purchase tender.</title>
<headline>India issues second Jan diesel purchase tender.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a second tender for the purchase of high speed diesel for delivery in January, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender requests offers of 40,000-45,000-tonne cargoes of 0.5 percent sulphur diesel for delivery to the west coast port of Kandla.</p>
<p>The tender closes on December 11 and offers should be valid until December 13.</p>
<p>Traders said IOC's new tender was due to its low award of only 255,000-tonnes in its first tender on November 22.  </p>
<p>Prior to the award, the market had initially estimated IOC requirement to be at least on par with its December purchase of 520,000-tonnes.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
